## Patterns to follow
- Every-problem-at-once error, `graph/errors.ts:1-10`:
  ```ts
  export class GraphError extends Error {
    readonly problems: string[];
    constructor(problems: string[]) {
      super(problems.length === 1 ? problems[0] : `Invalid task graph:\n${problems.map((p) => `  - ${p}`).join("\n")}`);
      this.name = "GraphError";
      this.problems = problems;
    }
  }
  ```
- zod issue formatting, `config/config.ts:80-87`: `` `${i.path.join(".")}: ${i.message}` `` (gives `repos: at least 2 repos`).
- A feature preflight failure prefixed by its name, `suite/orchestrator.ts:136-142`:
  ```ts
  try {
    await preflight({ cwd: opts.cwd, tasksDir: f.tasksDir, spec: f.prd, provider: opts.provider });
  } catch (err) {
    throw new Error(`${names[i]}: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`, { cause: err });
  }
  ```
- The single-repo apply and its log lines, `suite/orchestrator.ts:485-505` (`applyToCheckout`, `applied.ok`, `applied.files.length`, `applied.conflicts`, `log(\`  conflict: ${c}\`)`).
- Real paths: `realpathSync.native` (`launch/preflight.ts:133`) — needed on macOS (`/var` → `/private/var`) and for Windows junctions; compare paths only after it.
- Status writes always go through `store.update((s) => { … })`, which saves `suite.json` atomically.

## Step-by-step tasks

### CREATE `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/project.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**:
  ```ts
  export const PROJECT_FILE = "project.json";
  const NAME = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/;
  export const projectFileSchema = z.strictObject({
    name: z.string().regex(NAME, "use letters, digits, - and _"),
    repos: z.array(z.strictObject({ name: z.string().regex(NAME, "use letters, digits, - and _"), path: z.string().min(1) }))
      .min(2, "at least 2 repos"),
  });
  export interface ProjectRepo { name: string; path: string /* absolute, realpath */; tasksDir?: string /* abs, when tasks/<name>/ exists */; spec?: string /* abs specs/<name>.md */ }
  export interface Project { dir: string /* abs, realpath */; name: string; contract: string /* abs contract.md */; testPlan?: string /* abs test-plan.json when present */; repos: ProjectRepo[] }
  export class ProjectError extends Error { readonly problems: string[]; … }   // message: one problem as is, else `Invalid project <dir>/project.json:\n  - …`
  export async function loadProject(dir: string): Promise<Project>
  ```
  `loadProject`: resolve `dir` and take its `realpathSync.native` (missing folder → `ProjectError(["project folder not found: <dir>"])`); read `project.json` (missing → `no project.json in <dir>`, bad JSON → `invalid JSON in project.json: <msg>`); zod issues → `<path>: <message>`. Then, collecting problems instead of throwing:
  - each repo `i`: `path.resolve(dir, r.path)` must exist (`repos.<i>.path: <path> does not exist`), and its realpath must be the root of a git checkout: `isRepo(real)` and `realpathSync.native(await repoRoot(real)) === real` (`repos.<i>.path: <path> is not the root of a git checkout`); it must not be the project folder itself; duplicate names → `repos.<i>.name: duplicate repo name "<name>"`; two entries with the same realpath → `repos.<i>.path: <path> is the same repo as <other name>`;
  - `contract.md` missing → `contract.md is missing`;
  - `tasksDir = <dir>/tasks/<name>` when it is a directory; `spec = <dir>/specs/<name>.md` when it is a file; tasks without spec → `specs/<name>.md is missing (tasks/<name>/ exists)`; a `tasks/<x>/` folder whose name is no repo → `tasks/<x>/ matches no repo in project.json`;
  - no repo with tasks → `no repo has a tasks/<name>/ folder: nothing to change`;
  - `test-plan.json` present → `await loadTestPlan(dir)`, an error becomes `test-plan.json: <message>`.
  Throw `new ProjectError(problems)` when any; else return the `Project` with repos in `project.json` order. Messages always use `/` (`tasks/api/`), whatever the OS.
- **IMPORTS**: `existsSync`, `realpathSync`, `statSync` from `node:fs`; `readFile`, `readdir` from `node:fs/promises`; `z` from `zod`; `isRepo`, `repoRoot` from `../git/git.js`; `loadTestPlan` from `../graph/testPlan.js`.
- **GOTCHA**: the zod check on `repos` fails as a whole when it has one entry, so the per-repo checks run only when the schema passed. `realpathSync.native` resolves Windows junctions; never compare unresolved paths.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-execution -- suite/project`

### CREATE `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/joint.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT** (the stub a later task fills in; keep these exact names):
  ```ts
  export const jointDirOf = (suiteDir: string): string => path.join(suiteDir, "worktrees", "joint");
  export const jointRepoDir = (suiteDir: string, name: string): string => path.join(jointDirOf(suiteDir), "repos", name);
  export interface JointContext {
    suiteId: string; suiteDir: string; store: SuiteStore; log: (line: string) => void; project: Project;
    signal?: AbortSignal; reviewHub?: RetryHub; reviewEvents?: RunEmitter;
  }
  export interface JointResult {
    /** False: open findings remain; the suite ends `failed` and nothing is applied. */
    ok: boolean;
    /** The exit code when not ok, or with `keep`; EXIT_REVIEW_FAILED / EXIT_SUCCESS when omitted. */
    exitCode?: ExitCode;
    /** Set when the phase passed but nothing may be applied (dropped in the human review, code review not performed): the reason for the log. */
    keep?: string;
  }
  /** The joint phase across every repo on `suite/<rid>`. Stub: passes at once. */
  export async function jointPhase(_ctx: JointContext): Promise<JointResult> { return { ok: true }; }
  ```
