### UPDATE `packages/graph-execution/src/suite/orchestrator.ts`
This is where the multi-repo flow forks from the single-repo one. Keep every single-repo line as it is; add the branches below.
- **IMPLEMENT**:
  - `SuiteOptions` gains `project?: string` (the `--project` folder, relative to `cwd`). A project suite is called with `features: []` (so `serveSuite`'s `"features" in opts` test at line 558 still picks `runSuite`).
  - `SuiteContext` (lines 63–71) gains `project?: Project`. For a project suite `repo` is the project folder (the suite's home).
  - **Fork 1, start**: at the top of `startSuite` (line 147, before `validateSuite`): `if (opts.project !== undefined) return startProjectSuite(opts);`. New exported `validateProjectSuite(opts: Pick<SuiteOptions, "cwd" | "project" | "provider" | "merge" | "reviewers" | "env">): Promise<{ project: Project; reviewersFile?: string }>`: `loadProject(path.resolve(opts.cwd, opts.project))`; the project folder must be a git repo root (`isRepo` + realpath of `repoRoot` equals `project.dir`, else `UsageError("the project folder <dir> must be a git repository: run git init there")`); `suiteReviewersFile(opts.cwd, opts.reviewers, opts.env ?? process.env)`; then for each repo in `project.json` order, throwing `UsageError(\`${name}: …\`)` at the first problem: git identity (`assertGitIdentity(repo.path)`, message prefixed), has a commit (`resolveRef(path, "HEAD")`, `the repository has no commits yet`), `isDirty(repo.path, [RUNS_DIR])` → `working tree has uncommitted changes`, `currentBranch === "HEAD"` and `opts.merge` → `detached HEAD; check out a branch, or pass --no-merge`, and for a repo with tasks `preflight({ cwd: repo.path, tasksDir: repo.tasksDir, spec: repo.spec, provider: opts.provider, ...(reviewersFile ? { reviewers: reviewersFile } : {}) })` with the prefixed message as in lines 136–142. `startProjectSuite(opts)`: run `validateProjectSuite`; `ensureExcluded(project.dir, \`${RUNS_DIR}/\`)`; `loadConfig(project.dir)` gives `concurrency` and `humanReview` defaults (as lines 154–155, 179); create `suiteDirOf(project.dir, suiteId)` with `features/`, `logs/` and `specs/`; take the lock; copy the reviewers file as the single-repo start does; for every repo record `{ name, path, startingCommit: HEAD, startBranch? }` (omit `startBranch` on a detached HEAD); for every repo with tasks write `<suiteDir>/specs/<name>.md` = repo spec text trimmed at the end + `\n\n## Contract\n\n` + `contract.md` text, and create the feature `{ name: repo.name, tasksDir: repo.tasksDir, prd: <that spec file>, runId, status: "queued", repo: {…} }` (unique run ids as at lines 163–169); save the store with `project: { dir, name, contract }`, `repos`, `startingCommit` = the project folder's HEAD (`?? ""`), no top-level `startBranch`, `merge`, `humanReview`, `integration: { merged: [] }`; log `Suite <id>: <n> feature(s) in <repo names joined by ", ">, concurrency <c>`; `onReady`; return the context with `spawn: opts.spawn ?? defaultSpawnOf(opts.cliPath, project.dir)` and `project`. Release the lock on any error (lines 188–191).
  - **driveFeatures** (shared; only these changes): in `start()` pass the feature's repo as the spawn cwd in both branches: `spawn(args, env, logFile(f), f.repo?.path)`. In `sync()` (line 285) `integrate: !state.project && idle() && …`; in the request branch (line 387) add `!state.project &&` so "Start integration" (excluding failed features) never happens in a project suite. **Fork 2, after features**: line 405 becomes `if (outcome === "features-done") return await guarded(ctx, () => (ctx.project ? afterProjectFeatures(ctx, opts) : afterFeatures(ctx, opts)));`. In a project suite add `no repo was changed` to the `failed features: …` log line (line 410).
  - **Fork 3, resume**: in `resumeSuite`, right after the `already finished` check (line 211) and before `wasIntegrating` (line 213): `if (store.state.project) return await resumeProject(...)`, which reloads the project with `loadProject(store.state.project.dir)` and refuses (`UsageError("project.json changed since the suite started")`) when its repo names or realpaths differ from `store.state.repos`; checks `assertGitIdentity` per repo (prefixed); applies the same status reset as lines 214–217; logs, calls `onReady`, builds the context with `project`; then `every feature done ? guarded(ctx, () => afterProjectFeatures(ctx, opts)) : driveFeatures(ctx, opts)`. The single-repo resume path below stays untouched.
  - New `afterProjectFeatures(ctx, opts)`: `status = "integrating"`, `integrationBranch = suiteBranchOf(suiteId)`; for each `state.repos` entry without `refs/heads/suite/<rid>` (`resolveRef`): `createBranch(repo.path, <the feature run's integrationBranch from its state.json>, branch)` when the repo has a feature, else `createBranch(repo.path, repo.startingCommit, branch)`; log `<name>: suite/<rid> at <first 7 of the sha>`. Then `const joint = await jointPhase({ suiteId, suiteDir, store, log, project: ctx.project!, signal: opts.signal, reviewHub: opts.reviewHub, reviewEvents: opts.reviewEvents })`. `joint.keep` → status `done`, log `<keep>; results left on suite/<rid> in every repo`, return `joint.exitCode ?? EXIT_SUCCESS`. `!joint.ok` → status `failed`, log `joint review failed: open findings in <suiteDir>/reports; no repo was changed`, return `joint.exitCode ?? EXIT_REVIEW_FAILED`. Else `return applyProject(ctx)`.
  - New `applyProject(ctx)`: `!merge` → log `<name>: the result is on suite/<rid>` per repo, status `done`, exit 0. A repo without `startBranch` → log `not applying: <name> started on a detached HEAD; results left on suite/<rid> in every repo`, status `done`. Pre-apply check of every repo whose `applied` is unset: `currentBranch` must be `startBranch` (`<name>: the checkout is on <b>, not on <startBranch>`), `resolveRef(path, "HEAD")` must be `startingCommit` (`<name>: the checkout moved from <7 chars> to <7 chars> during the suite`), `!isDirty(path, [RUNS_DIR])` (`<name>: working tree has uncommitted changes`). Any problem → log each as `<problem>; results left on suite/<rid> in every repo`, status `done`, exit 0, nothing applied. Then, one repo at a time in `repos` order, skipping repos with `applied`: a repo without a feature is recorded `applied: { files: 0, conflicts: [] }` without touching git (log `<name>: unchanged`); otherwise `applyToCheckout(repo.path, repo.startBranch, branch)`; on `ok` save `repos[i].applied = { files: r.files.length, conflicts: r.conflicts }` immediately and log `<name>: applied suite/<rid> to <startBranch>: <n> files, <c> conflicts` plus `  conflict: <path>` lines; on `!ok` log `<name>: not applying: <reason>; the result is on suite/<rid>` and end `done` (repos applied before it stay applied: say so in the log). When all are applied: top-level `applied = { files: sum, conflicts: every conflict as "<name>/<path>" }`, status `applied`, exit 0.
  - `serveSuite` `onReady` (line 543): for a project suite the review repo is the suite's home, `path.resolve(dir, "..", "..")`, not `repoRoot(opts.cwd)` (the CLI may run from elsewhere): `repo: "project" in opts && opts.project !== undefined ? path.resolve(dir, "..", "..") : await repoRoot(opts.cwd)`.
- **IMPORTS**: `loadProject`, `type Project` from `./project.js`; `jointPhase` from `./joint.js`; `createBranch`, `isDirty`, `ensureExcluded` from `../git/git.js`; `EXIT_REVIEW_FAILED` from `../state/errors.js`; `RUNS_DIR` from `../state/paths.js`. Export the private `readRunState` from `suite/e2e.ts` (lines 35–40) and use it to read a feature run's `integrationBranch`.
- **GOTCHA**:
  - A resumed apply runs the pre-check only on repos without `applied`: an applied repo is dirty by design.
  - A feature run started in a repo must find its folder through `GRAPH_EXECUTION_RUNS_ROOT` (already set in `start()`), both fresh and on `--resume --run <id>` (`findRun` honours it).
  - `afterProjectFeatures` must be idempotent for resume: existing `suite/<rid>` branches are kept, applied repos are skipped.
  - No `integrate()` / `afterIntegration()` / `runE2e()` call may happen for a project suite.
  - Paths: build every path with `path.join`/`path.resolve`; only log and messages use `/`.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-execution -- suite/`

